In terms of the game itself I added a background to the main scene that starts the game. In the main scene you have two options, one is host (this goes to the server scene) and the other is player (this would be the
client scene). If you click on the host, it causes you to go to the server scene where you (as the host) have the ability to start the game. If you click on the player button (titled: unfortunate player) then you 
will go to the login screen where you enter in name and type. The login screen gives you the login info for the 4 characters you can choose from. It also has a little backstory to get you started on what the game
is about. Once you login and the host starts the game, it'll turn to a new scene where you see the questions and 4 buttons (4 different answers you can choose from). Once any player makes a choice whether right 
or wrong, the game will move on to the next question. If the player chooses right, the game will tell you that the player chose the right answer, if the player chose the wrong answer then it will tell you that you
chose the wrong answer. There are a total of 30 questions. Once all questions have been answered you will be led to the game over scene where you have the choice to start a new game or exit the game.

