In terms of parallel play, all players can play at the same time. In terms of if the game is fun to play, I would say it's pretty fun as some questions require thinking while other questions fit more with the theme.
The theme is a scary quiz game where the story is more or less like this: "You stumble across this game that tells you that you are chosen to play this game and you have no choice. If you play there's a chance to win,
if you don't play, you die. This forces the player to play and they will be asked questions in 3 different categories (riddle, history, horror). Once all 30 questions are answered they will go to the game over scene 
which tells them that it didn't matter if they beat other players by getting more qusetions right, they're soul is still trapped in this game and the only way to get it back would be to play again and win. This 
essentially forces players to keep player if they believe what the game says or risk dying if they don't believe what the game says.

